AEM Developer
Responsibilities
Develop and deliver Web experiences on AEM.
Collaborate with Management, analysts, designers, and clients to identify end-user requirements and specifications.
Develop complex components and templates in AEM with Touch UI using Sightly/HTL and modern front-end frameworks including Angular, React.js, Granite, and Coral UI Foundation Framework.
Participate in code reviews of ongoing projects and ensure code quality is at the highest level possible including using the appropriate design patterns.
Produce efficient and elegant code based on the requirements.
Test and deploy programs and applications.
Troubleshoot, debug, maintain, and improve existing software.
Assess user feedback to improve application performance.
Iterate over solutions in response to client feedback.
Contribute technical documentation to guide future development projects.
Participate in peer reviews and assess peer pull requests.
Learn new technology practices to improve support for existing and future projects.
Requirements
2+ years of experience:
Implementing AEM solution features, including templates and components, and configuring the Web console;
Working with enterprise content management systems;
Developing Web-based applications.
Proven experience as an Application Developer.
Familiarity with architectural styles and design patterns.
Excellent troubleshooting and communication skills.
Comprehensive understanding of Agile methodologies.
Ability to:
Work effectively on multiple tasks against shifting priorities;
Rapidly absorb complex technical and/or conceptual information;
Anticipate issues and provide solutions for complex problems.
Superior analytical and problem-solving skills.
Demonstrated competency with the following:
Key Adobe CQ/AEM APIs and functionality (Sites, Apps, Assets, Forms, Commerce, etc.);
Web technologies (CSS, HTML, JavaScript);
Use of component architecture and atomic design principles;
Mobile-first development and responsive design, following SEO and Accessibility Best Practices.
Experience with the following:
CSS preprocessors including Sass, SCSS, Less;
Adobe Experience Cloud, Analytics, Mobile Services, and LiveCycle;
Integrating applications with Web services including RESTful Web services;
Web architecture concepts (RESTful APIs, client-side data binding);
Working with Git (GitFlow is a plus);
Working with front-end build tools including Webpack;
Working with testing frameworks including Mocha or Jest;
Understanding and implementing automated testing and pre-commit checks including linting and style checking;
Working with the most up-to-date versions of front-end technologies.
Working knowledge of the following:
Marketing, communications, advertising, or related field;
Build & Deployment Automation using Jenkins, GitHub Actions, etc.;
Web performance optimization (RAIL or PRPL);
Java Server-side programming.
Experience working within a professional services firm, consulting firm, or agency.
This is a 12-month Contract with our Kansas City, MO client. Employee benefits include Medical/Dental Benefits, Paid time off, Paid Holidays, and a 401(k) plan (with an immediately vested company match) available through TriCom during the contract period. H-1 B visa sponsorship is not available for this position. No third-parties, please.
